            expression (stdlib/int32.mli[161,6100+0]..[175,6764+66])
              Pexp_constant PConst_string(" Convert the given string to a 32-bit integer.\n   The string is read in decimal (by default, or if the string\n   begins with [0u]) or in hexadecimal, octal or binary if the\n   string begins with [0x], [0o] or [0b] respectively.\n\n   The [0u] prefix reads the input as an unsigned integer in the range\n   [[0, 2*Int32.max_int+1]].  If the input exceeds {!Int32.max_int}\n   it is converted to the signed integer\n   [Int32.min_int + input - Int32.max_int - 1].\n\n   The [_] (underscore) character can appear anywhere in the string\n   and is ignored.\n   @raise Failure if the given string is not\n   a valid representation of an integer, or if the integer represented\n   exceeds the range of integers representable in type [int32]. ",(stdlib/int32.mli[161,6100+0]..[175,6764+66]),None)
